course: dictionary
lesson: 11384
title: Absorbent: what soaks things up
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Absorbent means able to soak up a liquid. You can work this out from the words around it: «The kitchen roll was very absorbent, and it soaked up the spilt juice in seconds.» Soaked up and spilt juice are the clues. The paper took the juice in, so absorbent must mean able to soak up liquid.
explain: Context can also show you what is not absorbent. «The plastic tray was not absorbent, so the water ran straight off it.» The clue is ran off. The water did not sink in, so the tray kept it on the top.
explain: Use the swap test to check. Put your meaning in place of the word: «The towel is able to soak up water» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Absorbent means able to soak up a liquid, like water, juice or milk.
fact: Absorbent is a describing word: «an absorbent towel», «The sponge is absorbent».
fact: Cotton, paper towel and sponges are absorbent. Plastic, foil and rubber are not.
fact: Absorb means to soak up or take in. Absorbent is the word that describes something that can do this.
fact: In science you can test which materials are absorbent by dropping water on them and seeing how much soaks in.
exercise: «The kitchen roll was very absorbent.» What does absorbent mean? | Very hot to touch | Shiny and smooth | Able to float on water | *Able to soak up liquid
exercise: Which material is absorbent? | Rubber | *Cotton | Foil | Plastic
exercise: «The plastic tray was not absorbent, so the water ran off it.» What does ran off show? | The tray was full of water | The water soaked into the tray | *The water did not soak in, it slid away | The water was hot
test: «The baby's nappy was very absorbent, so the bed stayed dry.» What does absorbent mean here? | Able to be seen from far away | Able to make a loud noise | Hard and heavy | *Able to soak up liquid
test: Which thing is NOT absorbent? | Cotton cloth | *Plastic bag | Paper towel | Sponge
exam: Ella says absorbent means waterproof. Which answer is correct? | Absorbent means shiny and smooth | Absorbent means able to soak up liquid, and waterproof means liquid cannot get through | Absorbent means very heavy | *Absorbent and waterproof mean exactly the same thing
